# literature review + methods + results

TITLE

A Hybrid Feature Selection and Autoencoder-Assisted XGBoost Model for Credit Card Fraud Detection

ABSTRACT

Credit card fraud detection is a critical problem due to the highly imbalanced
nature of financial transaction data. Traditional machine learning models often
fail to detect rare fraudulent transactions effectively. This paper proposes a
novel hybrid model named HFS-XGBoost-AE, which integrates hybrid feature
selection, unsupervised anomaly detection using autoencoders, and supervised
classification using XGBoost. Experimental results demonstrate that the proposed
method significantly improves recall and AUC compared to baseline models while
reducing false positives.

KEYWORDS

Fraud Detection, Autoencoder, XGBoost, Feature Selection, Imbalanced Data

1. INTRODUCTION

Credit card fraud causes substantial financial losses worldwide. The increasing
volume of online transactions demands intelligent and automated fraud detection
systems. However, the rarity of fraud events makes model training challenging.
This research addresses these challenges by combining deep learning-based anomaly
detection with ensemble learning.

